@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP ProjectForge. Basic Git/issue/board behavior belongs to separate ProjectForge, with independent user/resource authority.
title AFTER MVP — advanced model — Proposed LC-07 repository revision and review identities
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
top to bottom direction
class RepositoryRecord
class NativeRepository <<evaluated backend>>
class PullRequestContext {
 +sourceContext : RepositoryRefRevision
 +targetContext : RepositoryRefRevision
}
class ReviewEvidence
class CheckEvidence
class RepositoryMutationAttempt {
 +commandId : CommandId
 +expectedRefs : EvaluatedContext
 +observedOutcome : ActualOutcome
}
class TagReleaseRecord
RepositoryRecord ..> NativeRepository : native objects / authoritative refs
RepositoryRecord -- PullRequestContext
PullRequestContext -- ReviewEvidence : exact revision
PullRequestContext -- CheckEvidence : evaluated context
PullRequestContext -- RepositoryMutationAttempt
RepositoryRecord -- TagReleaseRecord : exact revision / asset references
note bottom of RepositoryMutationAttempt
 Native ref update and SQL metadata are not one automatic transaction.
 Unknown effects require attributable native reconciliation.
 Schema/cardinalities and backend remain proposed.
end note
@enduml
